{
  "formatVersion": 2,
  "title": "Push-button interface: one-key dimming and blind, scene storing",
  "description": "Each input of the interface is wired to a conventional push-button and has one function. The interface measures short and long presses itself: hold a key and release it. Input 2 dims on one key (short press toggles, long press dims brighter or darker in turn, release stops); input 3 moves the blind on one key (long press moves, the direction alternates, short press stops); input 4 recalls scene 1 with a short press and stores it with a long press (DPT 18.001), so each actuator keeps its current state as the new scene.",
